To solve this problem, we can draw the triangle and add in the auxiliary lines to define the bisector on the perimeter and the bisector on the area. We can then find the slope of each of these lines and take their dot product to find $\theta$. Finally, we can call the tangent of $\theta$ $\text{tan}\,\theta$ and return it.

